statement:
Let $k$ be a field [def-weil-field] and let $X$ be a scheme of finite type over $k$ [def-pc-scheme, def-weil-finite-type-morphism]. There exists a unique geometrically reduced closed subscheme $X^{
atural}\hookrightarrow X$ [def-weil-closed-immersion, def-pc-geometrically-irreducible] such that $X^{
atural}(L)=X(L)$ for every separable field extension $L/k$ [def-pc-field-extension], where $X(L)=\operatorname{Hom}_k(\operatorname{Spec}L,X)$. Here a possibly transcendental extension is separable if each finitely generated intermediate extension is separably generated, that is, finite separable over a purely transcendental extension of $k$. The construction is functorial: every $k$-morphism $f:X	o Y$ between finite-type schemes restricts uniquely to $f^{
atural}:X^{
atural}	o Y^{
atural}$, compatibly with composition and identities. The construction commutes with finite products over $k$ and with every separable field extension $K/k$: $(X	imes_kY)^{
atural}=X^{
atural}	imes_kY^{
atural}$ and $(X^{
atural})_K=(X_K)^{
atural}$ as closed subschemes [def-pc-base-change]. If $X$ is geometrically reduced, then $X^{
atural}=X$. If $X=G$ is an affine group scheme [def-sc-group-scheme], its structure maps restrict to make $G^{
atural}$ a geometrically reduced closed subgroup scheme [def-sc-group-scheme-subgroup]. The empty scheme is allowed; no perfectness, reducedness or smoothness of $X$ is assumed.
